1
00:00:01,639 --> 00:00:09,238
Chapter 57. Of whales in paint, in teeth, in wood, in sheet iron, in stone,

2
00:00:09,239 --> 00:00:13,079
in mountains, in stars.

3
00:00:13,080 --> 00:00:18,274
On Tower Hill, as you go down to the London docks, you may have seen a

4
00:00:18,275 --> 00:00:23,479
crippled beggar, or kedger, as the sailors say, holding a painted board

5
00:00:23,480 --> 00:00:28,518
before him, representing the tragic scene in which he lost his leg. There

6
00:00:28,519 --> 00:00:33,238
are three whales and three boats, and one of the boats, presumed to contain

7
00:00:33,239 --> 00:00:38,435
the missing leg in all its original integrity, is being crunched by the jaws

8
00:00:38,436 --> 00:00:44,359
of the foremost whale. Any time these 10 years, they tell me, has that man held

9
00:00:44,360 --> 00:00:49,558
up that picture, and exhibited that stump to an incredulous world? But the

10
00:00:49,559 --> 00:00:52,435
time of his justification has now come.

11
00:00:52,436 --> 00:00:57,318
His three whales are as good whales as were ever published in whopping at any

12
00:00:57,319 --> 00:01:02,198
rate, and his stump as unquestionable a stump as any you will find in the

13
00:01:02,199 --> 00:01:07,558
western clearings. But though forever mounted on that stump, never a stump

14
00:01:07,559 --> 00:01:12,838
speech does the poor whaleman make, but with downcast eyes stands rofully

15
00:01:12,839 --> 00:01:16,359
contemplating his own amputation.

16
00:01:16,360 --> 00:01:20,914
Throughout the Pacific and also in Nantucket and New Bedford and Sag

17
00:01:20,915 --> 00:01:26,274
Harbor, you will come across lively sketches of whales and whailing scenes

18
00:01:26,275 --> 00:01:31,719
graven by the fishermen themselves on sperm whale teeth or ladies busks rot

19
00:01:31,720 --> 00:01:36,679
out of the right whale bone or other like scrimshander articles as the

20
00:01:36,680 --> 00:01:41,958
whalemen call the numerous little ingenious contrivances they elaborately

21
00:01:41,959 --> 00:01:46,755
carve out of the rough material in their hours of ocean leisure.

22
00:01:46,756 --> 00:01:51,878
Some of them have little boxes of dentisticl looking implements specially

23
00:01:51,879 --> 00:01:56,755
intended for the scrimshandering business, but in general they toil with

24
00:01:56,756 --> 00:02:02,274
their jack knives alone, and with that almost omnipotent tool of the sailor,

25
00:02:02,275 --> 00:02:07,799
they will turn you out anything you please in the way of a mariner's fancy.

26
00:02:07,800 --> 00:02:12,594
Long exile from Christrysendom and civilization inevitably restores a man

27
00:02:12,595 --> 00:02:17,719
to that condition in which God placed him, i.e. e what is called savagery.

28
00:02:17,720 --> 00:02:22,999
Your true whale hunter is as much a savage as an irakqua. I myself am a

29
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:28,115
savage, owing no allegiance but to the king of the cannibals, and ready at any

30
00:02:28,116 --> 00:02:33,638
moment to rebel against him. Now, one of the peculiar characteristics of the

31
00:02:33,639 --> 00:02:39,238
savage in his domestic hours is his wonderful patience of industry. An

32
00:02:39,239 --> 00:02:44,274
ancient Hawaiian war club or spear paddle in its full multiplicity and

33
00:02:44,275 --> 00:02:49,958
elaboration of carving is as great a trophy of human perseverance as a Latin

34
00:02:49,959 --> 00:02:55,159
lexicon. For with but a bit of broken sea shell or a shark's tooth, that

35
00:02:55,160 --> 00:03:00,198
miraculous intricacy of wooden network has been achieved, and it has cost

36
00:03:00,199 --> 00:03:03,638
steady years of steady application.

37
00:03:03,639 --> 00:03:08,755
As with the Hawaiian savage, so with the whale sailor savage, with the same

38
00:03:08,756 --> 00:03:14,679
marvelous patience, and with the same single sharks tooth of his one poor jack

39
00:03:14,680 --> 00:03:20,435
knife, he will carve you a bit of bone sculpture, not quite as workmanlike, but

40
00:03:20,436 --> 00:03:26,039
as close packed in its maziness of design as the Greek savage Achilles

41
00:03:26,040 --> 00:03:32,198
shield, and full of barbaric spirit and suggestiveness as the prince of that

42
00:03:32,199 --> 00:03:36,594
fine old Dutch Savage Albertch Durer.

43
00:03:36,595 --> 00:03:42,198
Wooden whales or whales cut in profile out of the small dark slabs of the noble

44
00:03:42,199 --> 00:03:47,719
South Sea warwood are frequently met with in the folks of American whalers.

45
00:03:47,720 --> 00:03:50,999
Some of them are done with much accuracy.

46
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:56,198
At some old gable roofed country houses you will see brass whales hung by the

47
00:03:56,199 --> 00:03:59,399
tail for knockers to the roadside door.

48
00:03:59,400 --> 00:04:04,115
When the porter is sleepy, the anvil-headed whale would be best. But

49
00:04:04,116 --> 00:04:09,238
these knocking whales are seldom remarkable as faithful essays. On the

50
00:04:09,239 --> 00:04:14,115
spires of some old-fashioned churches, you will see sheet iron whales placed

51
00:04:14,116 --> 00:04:18,914
there for weathercocks, but they are so elevated, and besides that are to all

52
00:04:18,915 --> 00:04:23,958
intents and purposes so labeled with hands off, you cannot examine them

53
00:04:23,959 --> 00:04:27,558
closely enough to decide upon their merit.

54
00:04:27,559 --> 00:04:33,638
in bony riby regions of the earth where at the base of high broken cliffs masses

55
00:04:33,639 --> 00:04:38,755
of rock lie strewn in fantastic groupings upon the plane. You will often

56
00:04:38,756 --> 00:04:44,115
discover images as of the petrified forms of the Leviathan partly merged in

57
00:04:44,116 --> 00:04:50,435
grass which of a windy day breaks against them in a surf of green surges.

58
00:04:50,436 --> 00:04:54,755
Then again in mountainous countries where the traveler is continually

59
00:04:54,756 --> 00:05:00,679
girdled by amphitheatrical heights here and there from some lucky point of view

60
00:05:00,680 --> 00:05:05,558
you will catch passing glimpses of the profiles of whales defined along the

61
00:05:05,559 --> 00:05:10,999
undulating ridges. But you must be a thorough whaleman to see these sites.

62
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:15,638
And not only that, but if you wish to return to such a site again, you must be

63
00:05:15,639 --> 00:05:20,198
sure and take the exact intersecting latitude and longitude of your first

64
00:05:20,199 --> 00:05:26,198
standpoint, else so chance-like are such observations of the hills, that your

65
00:05:26,199 --> 00:05:31,479
precise previous standpoint would require a laborious rediscovery, like

66
00:05:31,480 --> 00:05:37,638
the Salom Islands, which still remain incognito, though once high rough Madana

67
00:05:37,639 --> 00:05:45,079
trod them, and old Figua chronicled Nor when expandingly lifted by your

68
00:05:45,080 --> 00:05:50,594
subject can you fail to trace out great whales in the starry heavens and boats

69
00:05:50,595 --> 00:05:55,878
in pursuit of them. As when long filled with thoughts of war the eastern nations

70
00:05:55,879 --> 00:06:01,079
saw armies locked in battle among the clouds. Thus at the north have I chased

71
00:06:01,080 --> 00:06:06,039
Leviathan round and round the pole with the revolutions of the bright points

72
00:06:06,040 --> 00:06:12,039
that first defined him to me. And beneath the eulgent Antarctic skies, I

73
00:06:12,040 --> 00:06:17,558
have boarded the Argo Navvice and joined the chase against the starry Satus far

74
00:06:17,559 --> 00:06:22,914
beyond the utmost stretch of Hydrris and the flying fish.

75
00:06:22,915 --> 00:06:29,079
With a frigot's anchors for my bridal bits and fies of harpoons for spurs,

76
00:06:29,080 --> 00:06:34,679
would I could mount that whale and leap the topmost skies to see whether the

77
00:06:34,680 --> 00:06:44,800
fabled heavens, with all their countless tents, really lie encamped beyond my mortal sight.
